The domain layer is pure Dart with no Flutter imports. It holds entities, repository interfaces, use cases, and strategies. Repositories and use cases return `Either<Failure, T>`.

## Use cases

Place **use cases** in `domain/use_cases/`. They are the ViewModel’s single application entry point for a cohesive flow (list, detail, search).

- One use case per cohesive flow (e.g. `LoadItemList`, `GetItemDetail`).
- Coordinate repositories and domain strategies — ViewModels must not orchestrate multiple domain dependencies.
- Return `Either<Failure, T>`; do not emit UI state or import Flutter.
- Keep them thin: delegate to repositories/strategies; do not duplicate rules that belong on entities.
- Prefer typed method parameters. Introduce a sealed **domain command** only when one use case class must handle several distinct operations.

```dart
// domain/use_cases/load_item_list.dart
class LoadItemList {
  const LoadItemList(this._repository);

  final ItemRepository _repository;

  Future<Either<Failure, List<Item>>> call({
    ItemCategory? category,
  }) async {
    final result = await _repository.getItemList();
    return switch (result) {
      Left(:final value) => Left(value),
      Right(:final value) => Right(
          (category == null
                  ? const AllItemFilter()
                  : CategoryItemFilter(category))
              .apply(value),
        ),
    };
  }
}
```

## Strategy pattern

Use **Strategy** for interchangeable **pure** algorithms. Define contracts in `domain/strategies/`; keep I/O out of strategies.

- Prefer a **sealed class** or `abstract interface class`.
- Select strategies via constructor injection or inside the use case — not via `if/else` type chains in Views.
- Name by behavior (`CategoryItemFilter`, `AllItemFilter`).
- **Data sources** (remote, cache) live in `data/sources/` and are repository collaborators, not domain strategies.

```dart
// domain/strategies/item_filter_strategy.dart
sealed class ItemFilterStrategy {
  const ItemFilterStrategy();
  List<Item> apply(List<Item> items);
}

final class AllItemFilter extends ItemFilterStrategy {
  const AllItemFilter();
  @override
  List<Item> apply(List<Item> items) => items;
}

final class CategoryItemFilter extends ItemFilterStrategy {
  const CategoryItemFilter(this.category);
  final ItemCategory category;

  @override
  List<Item> apply(List<Item> items) =>
      items.where((i) => i.categories.contains(category)).toList();
}
```
